  "comments": "KM Sub# from 1935 to 1965 with definitions<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/634ff50ac577d.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/634ff50ac577d.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n1942 Long top 2<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6340112a9516d.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6340112a9516d.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n1961 narrow &amp; wide dates<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/634014c0e3116.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/634014c0e3116.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nReference numbers:<br />\r\nKM#220.3: The coins struck in Philadelphia and San Francisco have a serif on the “4” of the date; the Lima and London coins do not.<br />\r\nKM#220.4: Dates 1941-44 have thick flat-top &quot;4&quot; without serifs. 1945 has narrow 4 like KM#220.5.<br />\r\nKM#220.5: 1942, 1944 AP, and all 1945-49 have narrow 4 without serif on the crossbar. 1944 without AP has flattop &quot;4&quot; like KM#220.4. Engraver&#039;s initials AP appear on wreath stems of some 1944-45, all 1946 and some 1947 coins. Varieties exist, including narrow and wide dates for 1956 and 1961 issues.",
